            <ArticleTitle>Glenoid fracture nonunion presenting as instability in a young athlete.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>738-40</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A case of a teenage athlete with a 4-year history of shoulder pain caused by glenoid fracture nonunion is presented. This individual had findings consistent with traumatic anterior shoulder instability as well as normal radiographs. Arthroscopy showed a nondisplaced glenoid fracture that was stabilized successfully through a deltopectoral approach.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
